From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 21:54:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1164/3799] soh: rename func_80ACDDE8 -> EnPart_SetupMotion

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: sActionFuncs[0]: gives the piece its randomised yaw, speed, gravity, spin rate and lifetime according to params, then advances to action 1.
Defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Part/z_en_part.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Part/z_en_part.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Part/z_en_part.c b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Part/z_en_part.c
index c47a46a21..1fb77b4b3 100644
--- a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Part/z_en_part.c
+++ b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Part/z_en_part.c
@@ -36,7 +36,8 @@ void EnPart_Init(Actor* thisx, PlayState* play) {
 void EnPart_Destroy(Actor* thisx, PlayState* play) {
 }
 
-void func_80ACDDE8(EnPart* this, PlayState* play) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_80ACDDE8: sActionFuncs[0]: gives the piece its randomised yaw, speed, gravity, spin rate and lifetime according to params, then advances to action 1.
+void EnPart_SetupMotion(EnPart* this, PlayState* play) {
     f32 sign = 1.0f;
 
     this->action = 1;
@@ -240,7 +241,7 @@ void func_80ACE7E8(EnPart* this, PlayState* play) {
 
 void EnPart_Update(Actor* thisx, PlayState* play) {
     static EnPartActionFunc sActionFuncs[] = {
-        func_80ACDDE8, func_80ACE13C, func_80ACE5B8, func_80ACE5C8, func_80ACE7E8,
+        EnPart_SetupMotion, func_80ACE13C, func_80ACE5B8, func_80ACE5C8, func_80ACE7E8,  // was func_80ACDDE8 [LLM:HIGH]
     };
 
     EnPart* this = (EnPart*)thisx;
